<p dir="auto"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://camo.githubusercontent.com/07a6e78663f3b416132bc94e0f60342524db12f9d78930b506573225babcb563/68747470733a2f2f706f73746373732e6769746875622e696f2f6175746f70726566697865722f6c6f676f2e737667"><img align="right" width="94" height="71" src="https://camo.githubusercontent.com/07a6e78663f3b416132bc94e0f60342524db12f9d78930b506573225babcb563/68747470733a2f2f706f73746373732e6769746875622e696f2f6175746f70726566697865722f6c6f676f2e737667" title="Autoprefixer logo by Anton Lovchikov" data-canonical-src="https://postcss.github.io/autoprefixer/logo.svg" style="max-width: 100%; height: auto; max-height: 71px;; aspect-ratio: 94 / 71; background-color: var(--bgColor-muted); border-radius: 6px" class="js-gh-image-fallback"></a></p>
<p dir="auto"><a href="https://github.com/postcss/postcss">PostCSS</a> plugin to parse CSS and add vendor prefixes to CSS rules using values
from <a href="https://caniuse.com/" rel="nofollow">Can I Use</a>. It is recommended by Google and used in Twitter and Alibaba.</p>
<p dir="auto">Write your CSS rules without vendor prefixes (in fact, forget about them
entirely):</p>
<div class="highlight highlight-source-css notranslate position-relative overflow-auto" dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="::placeholder {
  color: gray;
}

.image {
  width: stretch;
}"><pre>::<span class="pl-c1">placeholder</span> {
  <span class="pl-c1">color</span><span class="pl-kos">:</span> gray;
}

.<span class="pl-c1">image</span> {
  <span class="pl-c1">width</span><span class="pl-kos">:</span> stretch;
}</pre></div>
<p dir="auto">Autoprefixer will use the data based on current browser popularity and property
support to apply prefixes for you. You can try the <a href="https://autoprefixer.github.io/" rel="nofollow">interactive demo</a>
of Autoprefixer.</p>
<div class="highlight highlight-source-css notranslate position-relative overflow-auto" dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="::-moz-placeholder {
  color: gray;
}
::placeholder {
  color: gray;
}

